// Resources linked into runner.exe: the application manifest
// (src/runner.manifest). Built by windres in the Makefile's Windows branch.
//
// Why the manifest exists: activeCodePage UTF-8 makes UTF-8 the process's
// ANSI code page on Windows 10 version 1903 and later, so the command line,
// the environment and every narrow file API speak UTF-8, the encoding the
// engine holds all text in. Without it a non-ASCII -p prompt reached the
// tokenizer in cp1252 on a Western European system, and as "?" for anything
// cp1252 cannot spell. Older Windows ignores the element; src/compat.c reads
// the wide forms itself there.
//
// The rest of the manifest is the MSYS2 toolchain's default one, which this
// replaces: run as the invoking user, and name the Windows versions the
// program was written for, so the OS applies no compatibility shims.
//
// Numeric on purpose, so the script needs no Windows headers: 24 is
// RT_MANIFEST and 1 is CREATEPROCESS_MANIFEST_RESOURCE_ID (winuser.h).
//
// The language is not decoration. The MSYS2 compiler links that default
// manifest (default-manifest.o) with language 0, and GNU ld, merging the two,
// keeps the manifest that names a language and drops the one that does not
// (bfd/peXXigen.c, rsrc_sort_entries); two manifests without a language are
// duplicate leaves, and which survives is not a promise. 0x0409 is English
// (United States).
LANGUAGE 0x09, 0x01
1 24 "runner.manifest"
